<title>USA: Nellcor gets FDA OK for monitoring products.</title>
<headline>Nellcor gets FDA OK for monitoring products.</headline>
<dateline>PLEASANTON, Calif. 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nellcor Puritan Bennett Inc said Tuesday it received marketing clearance from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for two new patient safety monitoring products.</p>
<p>The regulatory approval covers the NPB-40 handheld pulse oximeter, which provides a low-cost solution for portable oxygen saturation monitoring in any clinical setting, and the NPB-4000 multiparameter monitor, which measures oxygen, non-invasive blood pressure, temperature and respiration, and serves as either a portable or bedside monitor.</p>
<p>U.S. revenue shipments of both products will begin in the third quarter, the company said.</p>
<p>(( -- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
